WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.152
Early Saturday morning, Katie and her mom walked to Pinker's Drugstore.

2
00:00:17.153 --> 00:00:22.280
Katie was wearing her captain cap and carrying Mr. Higgins' list.

3
00:00:22.281 --> 00:00:28.402
They went up and down the aisles, looking for the items they needed for the tornado shelter.

4
00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:31.880
"First aid cream," said Katie.

5
00:00:31.881 --> 00:00:36.659
"Got it!" said Mom, putting the tube in her shopping basket.

6
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.395
"Bandages and tape," said Katie.

7
00:00:40.396 --> 00:00:43.830
"Bandages and tape!" said Mom.

8
00:00:43.831 --> 00:00:45.587
Katie looked at her list.

9
00:00:45.588 --> 00:00:48.063
"One more thing," she said.

10
00:00:48.064 --> 00:00:51.511
"We need a box to put everything in."

11
00:00:51.512 --> 00:00:54.244
Mom reached up to a high shelf.

12
00:00:54.245 --> 00:00:58.684
"Here's one that's the perfect size!" she exclaimed.

13
00:00:58.685 --> 00:01:01.630
"Great!" said Katie.

14
00:01:01.631 --> 00:01:06.130
"Great teamwork!" said Mom.

15
00:01:06.131 --> 00:01:11.644
"Good morning, Debra. Hello, Katie," said Mrs. Pinker at the checkout.

16
00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:14.314
"What have you got here?"

17
00:01:14.315 --> 00:01:19.160
"Katie and I are making a first aid kit," Mom explained.

18
00:01:19.161 --> 00:01:23.538
"We're getting ready for tornado season," said Katie.

19
00:01:23.539 --> 00:01:27.281
"I hope the Pinker family is prepared."

20
00:01:27.282 --> 00:01:31.615
Mrs. Pinker laughed and put their things in Mom's bag.

21
00:01:31.616 --> 00:01:40.159
As Katie and her mom stepped out of the drugstore, they heard a familiar voice. "Katie! Aunt Debra!"

22
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.220
Katie looked across the street.

23
00:01:42.221 --> 00:01:45.467
"It's Luke," she said.

24
00:01:45.468 --> 00:01:51.838
Luke was sitting at a table in front of Aunt Sally's coffee shop, Fried Pie Heaven.

25
00:01:51.839 --> 00:01:55.041
He had taped a sign to the shop window:

26
00:01:55.042 --> 00:01:56.241
LIVE BAIT

27
00:01:56.242 --> 00:01:58.197
ONE DOZEN WET WORMS

28
00:01:58.198 --> 00:02:00.347
$1.00

29
00:02:00.348 --> 00:02:06.040
Luke reached into a big tub of ice and held up a plastic cup.

30
00:02:06.041 --> 00:02:10.205
"Would you like some worms?" he asked with a grin.

31
00:02:10.206 --> 00:02:15.610
"Sorry," said Katie. "We already ate. HA!"

32
00:02:15.611 --> 00:02:17.499
She looked into the tub.

33
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.421
"I hope you have enough," she said.

34
00:02:21.422 --> 00:02:25.025
"I don't have time for the bait business right now.

35
00:02:25.026 --> 00:02:29.335
I'm captain of the Donovan Tornado Safety Team."

36
00:02:29.336 --> 00:02:35.084
"Uh-oh, I forgot all about that," said Luke with a frown.

37
00:02:35.085 --> 00:02:38.899
"So you're not helping me dig worms anymore?"

38
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.683
Just then Aunt Sally pushed open the door of the coffee shop.

39
00:02:43.684 --> 00:02:48.459
The scent of pie and fresh coffee filled the air outside.

40
00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:51.189
"Good morning!" she exclaimed.

41
00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:54.482
Aunt Sally was Mom's sister.

42
00:02:54.483 --> 00:02:59.784
"Mr. Higgins told our class to get our families ready for tornado season.

43
00:02:59.785 --> 00:03:03.148
Luke forgot," tattled Katie.

44
00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:08.014
Aunt Sally laughed as she brushed the flour from her apron and said,

45
00:03:08.015 --> 00:03:12.832
"I guess if a tornado comes, we'll just blow away!"

46
00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:14.918
Mom and Luke laughed too.

47
00:03:14.919 --> 00:03:17.938
Katie frowned and shook her head.

48
00:03:17.939 --> 00:03:22.372
She was the only one who seemed to be taking this seriously.

49
00:03:22.373 --> 00:03:29.137
Meanwhile Joy and Dad were on the slope above the Donovan pond looking at trees.

50
00:03:29.138 --> 00:03:32.722
They had just stopped under two elms.

51
00:03:32.723 --> 00:03:35.852
"These two trees might work," said Dad.

52
00:03:35.853 --> 00:03:38.597
"Let's see how far apart they are."

53
00:03:38.598 --> 00:03:41.795
He took a tape measure from his tool belt.

54
00:03:41.796 --> 00:03:46.698
"Here, hold your end of the tape on this tree," he said to Joy.

55
00:03:46.699 --> 00:03:51.275
Then he walked to the other tree, pulling the tape as he went.

56
00:03:51.276 --> 00:03:56.789
"One meter and twenty centimeters. Perfect," he said.

57
00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:01.587
"And this is a perfect spot for a tree house," said Joy.

58
00:04:01.588 --> 00:04:07.555
"From here, we can see the pond, the house, the chicken coop—everything!"

59
00:04:07.556 --> 00:04:11.938
"The two trees will hold up the back of the tree house," he said.

60
00:04:11.939 --> 00:04:15.398
"And we'll use two posts to hold up the front."

61
00:04:15.399 --> 00:04:20.681
Joy turned toward the house and saw Katie and Magoo racing up the hill.

62
00:04:20.682 --> 00:04:23.868
"Katie and Mom are back," she said.

63
00:04:23.869 --> 00:04:27.010
"I saw you from the road," called Katie.

64
00:04:27.011 --> 00:04:30.301
"Are you going to build the tree house here?"

65
00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:34.415
"Isn't this a perfect spot?" said Joy.

66
00:04:34.416 --> 00:04:38.766
Katie nodded. "It's excellent," she said.

67
00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:43.605
"I'll be able to watch the storm clouds roll in from the southwest.

68
00:04:43.606 --> 00:04:47.026
That's where tornadoes come from, you know."

69
00:04:47.027 --> 00:04:50.877
She looked up into the clear blue sky.

70
00:04:50.878 --> 00:04:55.526
"Good work, team," she said and ran back down the hill.

71
00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:58.783
"We better get busy," said Dad.

72
00:04:58.784 --> 00:05:05.324
"That's right, partner!" said Joy.
